tude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Sound <span class=\"italic\">-ain</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Diphthongs like <span class=\"italci\">-ai</span> can be combined with a consonant to give a particular sound.<br/>The sound <span class=\"italic\">-ain</span> is often found at the end of a word.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Practice pronouncing the <span class=\"italic\">-ain</span> sound in the following words.<br/><br/>Example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"obtain\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"strain\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ascertain\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"stain\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"train\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" complain\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"explain\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" plain\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You stain something when it becomes dirty. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "A strain means a great effort to do something.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Stressing New Information", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Sentence stress gives English its <span class=\"strong\">rhythm</span> or \"beat\". <br/>   Word stress is emphasis on <span class=\"strong\">one syllable</span> within a <span class=\"strong\">word</span>.<br/> Sentence stress is emphasis on <span class=\"strong\">certain words</span> within a <span class=\"strong\">sentence</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">Content words</span> <ul><li>Content words are the important or key words in a sentence. They provide the meaning of the sentence.</li></ul>  <span class=\"strong\">Structure words</span> <ul><li>Structure words are not important words. They are small words that you use to make the sentence correct. </li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Stressing New Information", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You pronounce new information with more breath force, since it is more prominent. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": " We've <span class=\"strong\">all</span> been there before, and  I <span class=\"strong\">know</span> how overwhelming <span class=\"strong\">new environments</span> can be.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You won't obtain any <span class=\"strong\">favors</span> from  <span class=\"strong\">anyone</span> that way,  <span class=\"strong\">especially</span> from <span class=\"strong\">our</span> customers!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to obtain", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to get; to secure something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You won't obtain any favors from anyone if you stare at people.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in a conversation between restaurant employees.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "strain", "type": "name"}, {"content": "severe or excessive demand on someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Being rude puts a strain on the relationship between the waiter and customers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to ascertain", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to make sure of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You need to repeat the orders to ascertain you got it right.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to stain", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to discolor something with spots or streaks", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was eating spaghetti and now I have a stain on my shirt.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "plain", "type": "name"}, {"content": "obvious, easy to understand", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You should speak in plain English.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "In pairs, write a dialogue (8-10) lines using as many words with the -ain sound as you can (at least 5).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Try to write about manners and customs either in your country or another country you are familiar with.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your dialogue with the class.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Your classmates must listen for the -ain words and write them down.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about manners and customs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use and pronounce words like train.", "type": "text"}]}]}